 "details": {
  "title": "I Only Have Eyes for You",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet in A (B for the trumpet), concert A♯3 to E5, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, which follows Rod Stewart’s record seven steps lower, about 108: the refrain from the lead sheet, A A bridge A, then 16 bars of solo, the end of the second A, the bridge and the last A again with the sheet’s own ending. Where the guitar’s chords would rub the sheet’s note, the line takes the chord’s (G♯ over B minor, E♭ over C minor 9, C♯ over F♯7♭9). The record has a trumpet solo; this one is our own line over its changes, not the record’s. A short line opens where the record’s strings come in, and it closes over the ringing A major 9.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "Harry Warren and Al Dubin (1934)"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The refrain from the lead sheet on the Fret Finder page’s chords; the solo and the intro and closing lines are our own"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "A major concert (B for the trumpet), a fifth below Rod Stewart’s record"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, A A bridge A, solo, the end of the second A, bridge, last A, ending"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (oheyes-guitar.mp3), 3:07"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "Bar for bar with the Fret Finder page"
   ]
  ]
 }
